1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,075
Gain & Levels.

2
00:00:02,025 --> 00:00:06,575
The most important skill: setting gain correctly and reading the meters.

3
00:00:06,575 --> 00:00:08,712
Gain vs. Fader.

4
00:00:08,712 --> 00:00:11,125
Comparing GAIN and FADER.

5
00:00:11,125 --> 00:00:28,312
GAIN: Set ONCE at sound check GAIN: Boosts the mic signal into the console GAIN: Only change with sound lead OK GAIN: Knob at top-left of channel strip FADER: Used ALL through the service FADER: Controls how loud the channel is in the room FADER: Small, smooth moves FADER: Start near the 0 mark Setting Gain — 7 Steps.

6
00:00:28,312 --> 00:00:33,450
Press SELECT on the channel: The channel strip section now shows that channel's settings.

7
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:39,462
Press SOLO, put on headphones: You'll hear only that channel — perfect for checking level in isolation.

8
00:00:39,462 --> 00:00:45,875
Have them perform at real service level: Singer sings at Sunday volume, speaker speaks at sermon volume.

9
00:00:45,875 --> 00:00:50,150
Turn GAIN until meter is green, touching yellow: Slow turns.

10
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:53,862
Peaks just barely touching yellow on the loudest moments.

11
00:00:53,862 --> 00:00:55,537
Hitting red?

12
00:00:55,537 --> 00:00:59,337
Turn gain down: Red = distortion (clipping).

13
00:00:59,337 --> 00:01:02,812
Bring gain down until peaks return to green-yellow.

14
00:01:02,812 --> 00:01:09,475
Turn on Low Cut for voice mics: Press the Low Cut (HPF) button in the channel strip to filter out rumble.

15
00:01:09,475 --> 00:01:16,487
Press SOLO off, set fader near 0: Exit solo, bring fader to 0 mark, then adjust by ear in the room.

